# Both of these were held out by configuration that does not travel with the repository: the
# worktrees by .git/info/exclude, which is local to one clone, and the local settings by a global
# gitignore on one machine. A fresh clone elsewhere had neither, and would have committed a
# working copy and a file full of absolute paths.
